<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Farabundo Martí</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1893">1893</a>–<a href="/years/1932">1932</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Agustín Farabundo Martí</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agustín Farabundo Martí was a Salvadoran communist leader who had served as secretary to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augusto-cesar-sandino">Augusto César Sandino</a> in Nicaragua. He helped organise the peasant and indigenous uprising of January 1932 in western El <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a> but was arrested before it broke out and executed by firing squad on 1 February 1932. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> coalition formed in 1980, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/farabundo-marti-national-liberation-front">FMLN</a>, was named after him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/farabundo-marti.jpg" alt="Farabundo Martí" width="217" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Farabundomarti.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
